# Test and tooling dependencies, reinstalled by `npm ci` in CI.
# Never commit it: it is thousands of files of someone else's code, and it makes
# a one-line change in the diff impossible to review.
node_modules/
# package.json and package-lock.json are COMMITTED: CI installs from them via
# `npm ci`, and neither is a secret.

# A generated artefact from the integration harness. No script in package.json
# produces it any more -- the harness became a separate repository -- so this
# entry is kept only so a file left over from an older checkout cannot be
# committed by accident.
TEST_MATRIX.json

# Live server test reports, copied in from a run of the integration harness on a
# real machine. These are the most sensitive thing this repository can hold: a
# report records the framework and inventory stack of a live server and the
# in-game NAME of the player who ran the harness. Nothing in the test suite
reports/

# Upstream native databases, fetched by hand and never committed.
#
# natives_gta.json is 2.7 MB and natives_cfx.json is 535 kB of somebody else's
# release artefact. They are inputs to `npm run gen-natives`, not outputs of it,
# and FiveM ships a new build regularly enough that committing them would mean a
# multi-megabyte diff in every review that touched the realm check.
#
# What IS committed is tools/natives/natives.json: the 144 natives this library
# actually calls, each with the realm it is legal in. That is what CI reads, and
# CI never needs the network.
#
# To refresh after a FiveM update:
#   curl -sL -o tools/natives/natives_gta.json  https://runtime.fivem.net/doc/natives.json
#   curl -sL -o tools/natives/natives_cfx.json https://runtime.fivem.net/doc/natives_cfx.json
#   npm run gen-natives
#   npm run test:all
tools/natives/natives_gta.json
tools/natives/natives_cfx.json

# Editor/agent working state, not part of the library.
.zcode/
.zcodeignore